5. Explain the concept of feature scaling. Why is feature scaling required before training certain machine learning models?
Feature scaling is the process of normalizing or standardizing numerical features so they are on a similar scale.
It ensures that no feature dominates others simply because of its magnitude.

6. Explain what Standard Scaling (Standardization) means. What happens to the mean and standard deviation of the dataset after scaling?
Standard scaling transforms data so that it has:
Mean = 0
Standard deviation = 1
The formula is:
𝑧=𝑥−mean/standard deviation
After scaling:
The mean becomes 0
The standard deviation becomes 1
This helps models treat all features equally and improves numerical stability.


